# Line endings.
#
# The paper store is the authoritative data: its YAML carries LaTeX in literal
# block scalars, so the bytes on disk are content, not formatting. `core.autocrlf`
# defaults to `true` on Windows and would rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout, which
# makes the working copy depend on each machine's git configuration.
#
# Measured: ruamel normalises line breaks, so the parsed questions and the
# `content_hash` are unaffected today (14,258 literal blocks, 0 fields retain a
# newline after parsing). Pinning LF keeps the *bytes* reproducible as well, so
# the property holds by construction rather than by luck.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Provenance binaries are content-addressed, not text — never touch them.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary

# Large provenance files live in Git LFS (see docs/GIT-DATA.md).
# Patterns are inert until git-lfs is installed and `git lfs install` has run.
/.npee-math-papers/sources/**/source.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
/.npee-math-papers/captures/**/pages/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
